<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Shuja Durrani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1842">1842</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Shuja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani</a> was a ruler of the Durrani Empire, reigning from 1803 to 1809 and again from 1839 to 1842. Driven out by his brother Shah Mahmud and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barakzai-dynasty">Barakzai</a> chiefs, he lived for decades in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>. The British restored him to the throne in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-anglo-afghan-war">First Anglo-Afghan War</a>, but he was assassinated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> in 1842 after their retreat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shah-shuja-durrani.jpg" alt="Shah Shuja Durrani" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Print made by: Lowes Cato Dickinson After: Sir Vincent Eyre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lithograph_of_Shah_Shujah_in_1843.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
